      en: "Abydos Temple is a remarkable feature of the geography and culture of Egypt. One of the oldest cities of ancient Egypt, famous for the Temple of Seti I and the Abydos King List. Center of the Osiris cult. Temple of Seti I. Contains the Abydos King List. This site holds particular significance in the history of Egypt, from pharaonic heritage to modern times. Like many notable places in Egypt, it links the pharaonic heritage with present-day life along the Nile. Thus, this place contributes to the diverse profile of Egypt between the Sahara, the Nile, the Suez Canal and the Red Sea.",
