      en: "Coptic Cairo is a remarkable feature of the geography and culture of Egypt. A part of Old Cairo which encompasses the Babylon Fortress, the Coptic Museum, and numerous ancient churches. Home to the Hanging Church. Site of the ancient Babylon Fortress. Center of Egyptian Christianity. This site holds particular significance in the history of Egypt, from pharaonic heritage to modern times. Like many notable places in Egypt, it links the pharaonic heritage with present-day life along the Nile. Thus, this place contributes to the diverse profile of Egypt between the Sahara, the Nile, the Suez Canal and the Red Sea.",
