      en: "Citadel of Qaitbay is a remarkable feature of the geography and culture of Egypt. A 15th-century defensive fortress located on the Mediterranean sea coast in Alexandria. Built on the ruins of the Lighthouse of Alexandria. Completed in 1477. Part of the coastal defense. This site holds particular significance in the history of Egypt, from pharaonic heritage to modern times. Like many notable places in Egypt, it links the pharaonic heritage with present-day life along the Nile. Thus, this place contributes to the diverse profile of Egypt between the Sahara, the Nile, the Suez Canal and the Red Sea.",
